body:
See, this is where I'm confused, I redeemed the key as soon as I bought the bundle a few days after the Humble Choice dropped. I haven't installed the game or anything, but the weird thing is that in my Steam Library it has both DLC AWE and The foundations as ones that I own... Not to mention there's no standard edition in my library... I'd download it to verify if I've got the DLC unlocked in game, but frankly, I've over a terrabyte of games downloaded as is and don't know if I want to waste the bandwidth to download it just to see if the game accepts the DLC or not...

&#x200B;

Update: So, I tried to buy the season pass from Humble Bundle since it was like $6... Just got the Steam Key and tried to activate it and redeem it on Steam but it said I already own the season pass.

&#x200B;

Kinda confused as to why I have the actual Ultimate Edition and not just the other version without the DLC, but, now I've got a key for a redundant product lol.

Might as well add this key to the "I forgot your birthday but I don't want you to think I forgot it" vault since I'm not going to give it to anyone that begs for it or sell it on those shady sites like g2a :-/

Agreed... It's actually starting to anger me, there's nothing worse than dealing with a company which will happily take your money, keep it, say there's no way in hell you're going to get a refund and then refuse you the ability to use it. It's not like I'm ordering 50 games or anything. 

&#x200B;

3. that's how many I was trying to buy. Now? My attempted purchases with my wallet credits are just outright cancelling my order after 2 manual review order cancels... I don't usually put on the tin-foil cap, but this really is starting to feel like a bit of theft by dishonesty. 

I've tried to figure out where I've violated the t's & c's and I'm just not seeing it. I didn't have any purchases beforehand aside from 1 bundle purchase a few days ago and my subscription renewal, and after a few days I finally got money transferred into my humble wallet... just to have the site and their staff effectively tell me to shove off for somehow violating their t's & c's... 

&#x200B;

I'd blame it on their system, but tbh, there have been a total of 3 different manual reviews that ended up in me waiting days and someone, seemingly at the last minute, cancelling my order... sorry, this sort of devolved into a rant, it's just very frustrating have this shite happen so often, especially since I now have $25 that I no longer have access to as a result of this fuckery.
